## Metadata
- Author: [[Matt Barnum]]
- Full Title: Nearly a Decade Later, Did the Common Core Work? New Research Offers Clues
- Category: #articles
- Summary:: A new study suggests that the Common Core State Standards may not have improved student learning in the U.S., showing declines in reading and math scores over time. Researchers found that states that adopted the standards did not perform better on federal tests compared to others. The challenges of implementing these changes may have contributed to the disappointing results.
- URL: https://www.chalkbeat.org/2019/4/29/21121004/nearly-a-decade-later-did-the-common-core-work-new-research-offers-clues/

## Highlights
- There’s very little other research on the Common Core. A 2015 Kentucky [study](https://caldercenter.org/sites/default/files/WP%20127_0.pdf) showed students who were exposed to the standards made larger gains than students who weren’t. ([View Highlight](https://read.readwise.io/read/01j80zz6d416ec28ywat7vqjm0))
    - Note: Why are we breezing over this fact?
- In New York City, for instance, teachers [didn’t get](https://www.chalkbeat.org/posts/ny/2013/09/05/many-teachers-still-waiting-on-textbooks-for-new-city-curriculum/) textbooks aligned to the new standards on time. In Massachusetts, [teachers said](https://hechingerreport.org/teachers-ready-common-core/) their training was simply low quality. Across the country, [teachers said](https://www.chalkbeat.org/posts/ny/2014/06/11/support-wanes-for-common-cores-high-stakes-for-new-york-teachers/) that implementing a new set of standards and state tests at the same time as new high-stakes teacher evaluation systems was untenable. These challenges are one obvious potential reason for the results of Song’s study. ([View Highlight](https://read.readwise.io/read/01j8100pp2y6j4s4y05841jaga))
- That leaves Song puzzled. *“*I don’t have a good hypothesis for why the effects actually grow over time,” she said. “That’s something I didn’t expect.” ([View Highlight](https://read.readwise.io/read/01j8101n5prz29dvq7cyrcpk02))


